The ipq60xx eMMC boards (jdcloud re-cs-02, re-cs-07, re-ss-01 and link
nn6000 v1/v2) mount their overlay from an F2FS volume in a loop device
that starts right after the squashfs on the rootfs partition, so every
sysupgrade rewrites the partition the system is running from.

do_stage2 only moves the configuration archive to flash when
platform_copy_config() is defined. ipq60xx never defined it, so the
archive stayed in tmpfs, disappeared when the system went down for the
upgrade, and the new overlay was formatted from scratch - "keep
configuration" was silently ignored and the device came up with factory
defaults.

emmc_copy_config() in lib/upgrade/emmc.sh already does the right thing
(writes the archive right after the newly written rootfs, where fstools
looks for its gzip header on the next boot), and ipq807x wires it up the
same way. Add the missing hook for the eMMC devices.

Tested on JDCloud RE-CS-02 (ipq6010): after this change, sysupgrade with
"keep configuration" restores /etc on the next boot.

Signed-off-by: Zang Baiyue <zcracker@163.com>
--- /target/linux/qualcommax/ipq60xx/base-files/lib/upgrade/platform.sh
+++ /target/linux/qualcommax/ipq60xx/base-files/lib/upgrade/platform.sh
@@ -307,3 +307,15 @@
 		;;
 	esac
 }
+
+platform_copy_config() {
+	case "$(board_name)" in
+	jdcloud,re-cs-02|\
+	jdcloud,re-cs-07|\
+	jdcloud,re-ss-01|\
+	link,nn6000-v1|\
+	link,nn6000-v2)
+		emmc_copy_config
+		;;
+	esac
+}
